From f879e9692305c032e52871cef8b40fc8733b74a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:47:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: bring-up diagnostics for Mahua's core and pipe
 check

HP's video firmware refuses every session on the HP OmniBook 5 (Mahua):
"Configured core N is not supported, Monitor=88000800", where Monitor is
the wrapper's efuse word. The Glymur platform data powers two cores and
sends four pipes. Add default-off module parameters to try the
alternatives on one boot:

  diag_cores    video cores to power and use (command line only)
  diag_pipes    HFI_PROP_PIPE for new sessions
  diag_core_id  HFI_PROP_CORE_ID for new sessions (0: not sent)

and log the efuse word and the core power status after the firmware
boots when any of them is set. Not for upstream.
